Over the past eight weeks in the Power Learn Project (PLP) Data Analytics track, I wrapped up my end-to-end capstone analyzing H1 2026 retail sales performance for Duka Electronics—from raw data quality auditing and SQL modeling to statistical testing and a Looker Studio dashboard.

A few highlights from the analysis:
• Branch divergence: Nairobi leads total revenue volume, while Eldoret recorded strong Q1-to-Q2 growth, and secondary branches saw Q2 pullbacks driven by repeat order frequency.
• Product mix trade-offs: High-ticket devices drive major top-line revenue from fewer orders, while accessories support strong margin and order counts.
• Statistical check: A Mann-Whitney U test (p < 0.001) confirmed higher per-order spend among higher loyalty tiers, reinforcing targeted retention over blanket discounting.

